Fill in A9-A11 iPhone/iPad device data generically

- Find wlan, bluetooth and multi-touch below /arm-io directly or below the
  UART/SPI node that hosts them (A9-A11 put them below e.g. uart2).
- The Wi-Fi antenna SKU is optional: iPhones and iPads have none. The MAC
  addresses for wifi0 and bluetooth0 come from the generic /chosen loop.
- Publish the NVMe host memory buffer iBoot reserved (ADT nvme-mmu0
  sart-region) into the nvme-hmb reserved-memory node.
- Copy touchscreen calibration (touchscreen0 alias) the same way as the
  touch bar's, skipping unprovisioned "syscfg/" references.

Replaces the J71b-only patch: no board compatibles are checked.

